[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1151/images/109832/109832-1791410089-169875235.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]Melee kill moves far more often, and every one of them in turn.[/b][/size]

[youtube]WFnghGRkrW4[/youtube]
[youtube]TenusopIUFg[/youtube][/center]

[size=4][b]In short[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fighters try grabs and kill moves about 8 times as often as the game lets them.[/*]
[*]A target at 30% health or less can be finished early, on half the swings; the victim dies in the animation.[/*]
[*]NPCs finish NPCs, and you finish them. Against you it stays the game's own rule.[/*]
[*]Every kill move a weapon can do is equally likely, so the same one stops repeating.[/*]
[*]All of it is a slider in MCM.[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex or MO2; manual installs are not supported. The installer checks your setup first.
Needs: Fallout 4 1.10.163, next-gen or the Anniversary Edition, [url=https://f4se.silverlock.org/]F4SE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url] (one DLL for every game version). [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/21497]MCM[/url] is optional but recommended: the settings page and a test button.
No masters beyond Fallout4.esm. Finishers.esp is a light plugin with no record overrides: it only carries the MCM page and two factions for the test fight.

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1151/images/109832/109832-1791410100-465715333.jpg[/img]
[b]Not only the last blow.[/b] The game plays a kill move only when it predicts that exact swing kills, and a raider even tries a grab or kill move just 1 time in 10, every 5 seconds. With Finishers, fighters try at least half the time, every 3 seconds, and a target at 30% health or less can be finished on half the swings.

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1151/images/109832/109832-1791410112-1740229034.jpg[/img]
[b]Every kill move in turn.[/b] The game plays the first kill move in a weapon's list whose roll passes, so Far Harbor's throat slash took half of all one-handed blade kill moves. At game start Finishers orders each list and evens out the rolls: 20 lists and 61 kill moves, creatures included. Paired moves that do not kill (shoves, tackles) keep the game's odds. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6691]How it works →[/url]

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Want to see it at once? MCM > Finishers > Testing > [i]Start a fight here[/i] spawns two melee raiders that fight only each other.[/*]
[*]You are never finished early: against the player, kill moves follow the game's own rule.[/*]
[*]Finishers overrides no records, so it can sit anywhere in your load order.[/*]
[/list]Source: [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-finishers]github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-finishers[/url] (MIT).
Finishers.dll is [url=https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/83dc109ccfeb387c85b7e69b1a8f95190f0b2913d462c203dbe84e002cecac7a]clean on VirusTotal[/url] (0/70).
